{
  "abstract": "We present the first measurement of midrapidity vector meson \u03c6 production in Au+Au collisions at RHIC (sNN=130\u2002GeV) from the STAR detector. For the 11% highest multiplicity collisions, the slope parameter from an exponential fit to the transverse mass distribution is T=379\u00b150(stat)\u00b145(syst)\u2002MeV, the yield dN/dy=5.73\u00b10.37(stat)\u00b10.69(syst) per event, and the ratio N\u03c6/Nh\u2212 is found to be 0.021\u00b10.001(stat)\u00b10.004(syst). The measured ratio N\u03c6/Nh\u2212 and T for the \u03c6 meson at midrapidity do not change for the selected multiplicity bins.",
